          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "pdu_408_build writes the payload marker without checking capacity\n\npdu_408_build() ignores the return values of coap_add_token() and coap_add_option_internal() and then unconditionally writes COAP_PAYLOAD_START at pdu->token[pdu->used_size++], so it writes one byte past the heap allocation whenever the token exactly fills the PDU. The defect is real, but the previously claimed remote trigger is not reachable in the default configuration: a Q-Block1 request must also carry Size1 and RTag options plus a URI path to reach this path, and with the default 1152-byte UDP MTU the session PDU is about 1148 bytes, so a token large enough to fill used_size leaves no room for those mandatory options; the request either omits them and is rejected with 4.00, or exceeds the MTU and is rejected during parsing, before pdu_408_build() runs. Reachability is limited to a build or transport that admits a PDU-filling token together with the mandatory Q-Block options, or to future caller misuse; no such trigger was demonstrated.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Memory corruption\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-787\n\nRemediation:\nCheck both coap_add_token() and coap_add_option_internal() results. Call coap_pdu_check_resize(pdu, pdu->used_size + 1) before writing the marker; on failure, delete the PDU and return NULL so the caller defers the 4.08.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Under a build or transport that admits a maximum-size token alongside Q-Block1 Size1 and RTag options, send a Q-Block1 request with missing blocks and run under ASan; verify no heap-buffer-overflow.\n- Add a unit test for pdu_408_build with a token that exactly fills the PDU.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Always route payload marker insertion through a helper that performs a capacity check."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:76b66fa387c068682cb20a1223a0c1ac4d9a92f131c73a9700bc9c99fd483f4d"
          },
