          "message": {
            "text": "Short OSCORE responses advance the replay window without rollback\n\nFor a response carrying a Partial IV, coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu() validates and advances rcp_ctx->last_seq before AEAD verification. If the ciphertext is too short, where encrypt_len <= tag_len, the response branch jumps to error without calling oscore_roll_back_seq(), unlike the request branch and the generic decrypt-failure path. An on-path attacker can forge a high-PIV short response that matches the token and association, causing later legitimate responses with lower PIVs to be rejected as replays.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Denial of service\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-400\n\nRemediation:\nCall oscore_roll_back_seq(rcp_ctx) on every response decryption failure, including the encrypt_len <= tag_len case, or defer last_seq updates until after successful AEAD verification."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:a533be60cd90b5f956f082e5bd97c87129a0ef7a17e457c6fdb2c25442e54d11"
          },
