          "message": {
            "text": "Uri-Path-Abbrev fallback retransmit drops the request body\n\nWhen a server has rejected Uri-Path-Abbrev, coap_send() duplicates the request with the abbreviation expanded into new. The payload is then appended to the original pdu via coap_add_data(pdu, ...), not to new, and the original is deleted. The duplicate contains options but no payload, so the retransmitted request silently loses its body.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Data integrity\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-670\n\nRemediation:\nCall coap_add_data(new, data_len, data) and handle failure by deleting new and returning an error. If the duplicate helper is expected to preserve payload, extend it to copy data explicitly.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Send a PUT with Uri-Path-Abbrev and a body to a peer that rejects the option; assert the retransmitted datagram contains the payload marker and body.\n- Add a regression test around coap_pdu_duplicate_lkd with a body-bearing PDU.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Make coap_pdu_duplicate_lkd() copy data explicitly or document that callers must add it to the returned PDU."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:6104851a45152a29060c9914f6eab663af9f7f9a0ab4506dcf252d777aee4060"
          },
          "properties": {
