          "message": {
            "text": "OSCORE external credential lookup can return a context with no recipient and crash the server\n\nWhen an application registers an external credential callback with coap_oscore_register_external_handlers() and the callback returns a configuration with multiple recipients, oscore_find_context() assigns *recipient_ctx only when a recipient matches the request KID. If none matches, it frees every recipient, leaves *recipient_ctx NULL, sets tmp_ctx->recipient_chain = NULL, and still returns the context. coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu() then calls coap_oscore_session_set_recipient_ctx(session, NULL), which is a no-op, and dereferences rcp_ctx->initial_state, crashing on a single unauthenticated OSCORE request with an unknown KID.\n\nSeverity: high\n\nCategory: Null pointer dereference\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-476\n\nRemediation:\nInitialize *recipient_ctx = NULL at the start of the callback path and return NULL when no recipient matches, freeing the temporary context. Reject the request when osc_ctx is non-NULL but rcp_ctx is NULL before storing or dereferencing the recipient."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:d5b9f600e60c65f126fd23d4cb4b608c5aa27bc50a23977653a4b7e78027c071"
          },
          "properties": {
