          "message": {
            "text": "Block1 reassembly can hand uninitialized heap bytes to the application\n\ncoap_block_build_body_lkd() allocates a body of total bytes with coap_new_binary() and copies only each received segment at its offset. If a client changes SZX between blocks so the next offset jumps past data already received, the gap is never initialized. give_app_data later sets pdu->body_data to that buffer and pdu->body_length to total_len, so an application that returns the body, such as an echo or proxy resource, discloses heap contents.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Information disclosure\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-457, CWE-200\n\nRemediation:\nZero-initialize the body allocation, or track received byte ranges and reject any Block1 sequence with a gap or overlap. Compute offsets from the SZX established for the transfer and require each segment to start at the next expected byte."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:144918374a2e21d1b6507f769fdcf1a26b90fe8e996c40a872d435e54f90eaf0"
          },
