          "message": {
            "text": "WebSocket close path can overflow a 100-byte stack buffer with a partial frame\n\ncoap_ws_close() drains pending input into uint8_t buf[100] by calling coap_ws_read(session, buf, 100). If a large binary frame was only partially consumed, all_hdr_in remains set and data_ofs < data_size; coap_ws_read() skips the header-time size check and calls l_read(&data[data_ofs], data_size - data_ofs), so a peer that supplies the remaining frame bytes during the 1 ms drain windows writes attacker-controlled data past buf.\n\nSeverity: high\n\nCategory: Memory corruption\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-121, CWE-787\n\nRemediation:\nClamp the continuation read to min(data_size - data_ofs, datalen) and reject the frame if it cannot fit; in coap_ws_close(), size the drain buffer for the maximum accepted frame or do not call coap_ws_read with a smaller buffer."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:8716a6cef3b8408ba7fdd4f420d5d9e8fca8fe2e1dc1085603a09fa27e971f7f"
          },
