          "message": {
            "text": "OSCORE Appendix B.2 kid_context encoder writes past the 255-byte stack buffer and underflows its remaining-space counter\n\noscore_encode_option_value() points the CBOR writer at option_buffer[offset+1] but passes rem_space unchanged. The bytes actually available at that pointer are rem_space - 1. When the CBOR header plus kid_context length equals rem_space, oscore_cbor_put_bytes() writes the final byte to option_buffer[255], one past the 255-byte stack array, and the following rem_space -= 1 underflows to SIZE_MAX. The key-id bound check is then bypassed, memcpy(&option_buffer[offset], key_id, ...) writes past the array, and the returned offset of 256 or more is passed to coap_insert_option(), which reads past the stack array. The encoder runs when Appendix B.2 is configured and b_2_step is not NONE, with attacker-influenced kid_context bytes.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Memory corruption\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-787, CWE-193\n\nRemediation:\nPass rem_space - 1 to oscore_cbor_put_bytes() and require rem_space > 1; check nb + kid_context.length against the true remaining capacity, guard the rem_space decrement against underflow, and derive the next offset from the bounded return value."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:81546853c4c5077a56b4e35b8b88b3a8a932afef4db2c860b36c5c2227286626"
          },
