          "message": {
            "text": "Appendix B.2 creates unbounded OSCORE contexts before authentication\n\nIn Appendix B.2 mode, coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu() duplicates the OSCORE context for a request carrying an unknown kid_context and links it into context->p_osc_ctx before the AEAD tag is verified. The decryption-failure and error paths free only the PDU and associations, never the duplicated context. Repeated requests with unique kid_context values accumulate contexts, each holding a copy of the master secret, salt, and derived keys, until memory is exhausted.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Resource exhaustion\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-770\n\nRemediation:\nDo not attach the duplicated context until the AEAD tag verifies, or explicitly free and unlink it on every decryption failure. Add a bound on the number of B.2 contexts and expire idle ones."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:54afcb6ce8c30d79bf7aff039eed19d5473f424bacff9cfd78c955cea862a2fc"
          },
          "properties": {
